#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# SERVE THE PAINT PAGE -- two canvases and a terminal -- over TLS.
#
#     etcs modules/PaintProvider/scripts/serve_paint.etcs
#     then open https://localhost:8443/
#
# FROM ANY DIRECTORY, and that is a fix rather than a convenience. Every path
# below used to be relative to the process's working directory -- which is not
# a property of this script and not something it can check. Run it from
# anywhere else and each MountFile refused, the page still answered 200 from
# whatever else sat at that URL, and the first thing to notice was a script
# thread dying with nothing pointing back here. The one that matters is
# render_frames.etcs: it is the frame pump, so losing it leaves a black canvas
# and a runtime that is otherwise working perfectly. ACE_ROOT resolves the same
# way it does in the #IMPORT above (core/CommandExecutor.h).
#
# Same shape as WindowProvider's serve_web.etcs, and for the same reasons: one
# FileHtmlPage child (two StaticHtmlPage siblings under one server is a coin
# flip the hash re-tosses -- see that script), the two isolation headers without
# which a -pthread build's Workers die on `wasmMemory is undefined`, and every
# script MOUNTED at the path it is fetched from rather than copied into www/.
#
# ONE SERVER AT A TIME on 8443. This page and the window page are two views of
# the same runtime, not two services.

spawn NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
web.SetPort(8443)
web.EnableTLS(/tmp/etcs-cert.pem /tmp/etcs-key.pem)

# Cross-origin isolation, which is what makes SharedArrayBuffer -- and therefore
# threads -- available at all. Confirm from the page's console with
# `crossOriginIsolated, typeof SharedArrayBuffer`: true / "function".
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy same-origin)
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy require-corp)

web.spawn(NetworkProvider::FileHtmlPage tree)
tree.LoadFromDisk(ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/www)
tree.SetDefaultExtension(.html)

# ── the mounts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Each at the path the page stages it under (www/modules.json), which is the path
# the OS side reads it from -- so boot_paint_panels.etcs's `detach` and `run`
# lines are spelled once for both substrates instead of twice.
tree.MountFile(paint_routed_pointer.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_routed_pointer.etcs)
tree.MountFile(PaintProvider/scripts/paint_toolbar.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_toolbar.etcs)
tree.MountFile(PaintProvider/scripts/paint_wheel.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_wheel.etcs)
tree.MountFile(PaintProvider/scripts/paint_menu.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_menu.etcs)
tree.MountFile(PaintProvider/scripts/paint_layers.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_layers.etcs)
tree.MountFile(PaintProvider/scripts/paint_import.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_import.etcs)
tree.MountFile(RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs)

# The terminal view, from ShellProvider's own page rather than a copy of it.
# Mounted at "shell", which is what index.html's iframe points at; the MIME comes
# from the disk name.
tree.MountFile(shell ACE_ROOT/modules/ShellProvider/scripts/www/index.html)

# The whole served surface, which is the fastest way to catch a staging mistake:
# a name the page asks for and this does not list is a 404 waiting to happen.
# Worth reading every time the page misbehaves: a mount that failed says so here
# by being absent, and MountFile logged the path it could not open.
tree.ListPaths()

web.Start()
web.IsStarted()
